The cyclotomic surviving length and Serre. In any first-strand cyclotomic quotient containing $S$, the relation $x_1^{\lambda_i}$ kills precisely when the first-dot index $\epsilon_i^L(S)$ is at most $\lambda_i$; reading the formula of step 3.1 at the level of $G_0$ gives the actual surviving lowering length $\lambda_i+\epsilon_i(S)-\langle h_i,\beta\rangle$ for the right operator, and the same count at the first end by symmetry. The linear divided restriction operators on $G_0$ satisfy the quantum Serre relation by
[[thm-klr-projective-grothendieck-group-satisfies-the-negative-quantum-serre-relations]];
the simple-socle operators $e_i,f_i$ themselves are not claimed to satisfy a linear Serre identity. No positive-dominant label assumption on the original $P$ is made, since every weight comparison took place in the auxiliary finite-support datum of [F2].

